  "prompt_prefix": "/deep-research ",
  "instruction": "Of the top 5 states that have the most deaths by car crash in 2023, which had a seat belt use of less than 90% in 2023?",
  "answer": "Based on the research, here are the findings:\n\n## Top 5 States by Motor Vehicle Crash Deaths (2023)\n\n| State | Fatalities (2023) | Seat Belt Use (2023) | Below 90%? |\n|-------|-------------------|---------------------|------------|\n| Texas | 4,291 | 90.6% | No |\n| California | 4,061 | 96.2% | No |\n| **Florida** | **3,396** | **89.4%** | **Yes** |\n| **Georgia** | **1,615** | **87.6%** | **Yes** |\n| North Carolina | 1,561 | 92.2% | No |\n\n## Answer\n\n**Florida (89.4%) and Georgia (87.6%)** are the two states among the top 5 by crash deaths in 2023 that had seat belt use rates below 90% in 2023.\n\n## Sources\n\n1. **Fatality data**: NHTSA FARS 2023 ARF, \"State Traffic Data\" (DOT HS 813 743) — https://crashstats.nhtsa.dot.gov/Api/Public/ViewPublication/813743\n2. **Seat belt data**: NHTSA NOPUS 2023, \"Seat Belt Use in 2023 — Overall Results\" (DOT HS 813 615) — https://crashstats.nhtsa.dot.gov/Api/Public/ViewPublication/813615\n3. **Cross-verified fatalities**: IIHS Fatality Facts 2023 (state-by-state) — https://web.archive.org/web/2025/https://www.iihs.org/research-areas/fatality-statistics/detail/state-by-state\n4. **Cross-verified fatalities**: CDC WONDER 2023 motor vehicle traffic deaths — https://wonder.cdc.gov/mcd-icd10.html",
  "answer_chars": 1237,
  "expected_answer": "Florida, Georgia",
